          {
            title: 'Charlemagne',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Charlemagne is a trick-taking card game that involves tricks, trump, following suit. The game originated in Europe and has become popular worldwide.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Eastern Canada and Maine (USA). Euchre-based trick-taking; 4 players in fixed partnerships. Canadian form uses 34-card pack (Aâ€“7) plus two Jokers as top trumps; US form uses no Jokers, trump 9 as top. Single round of bidding; kitty of two cards.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '4 players, two against two, partners opposite. Deal and play clockwise.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '34-card pack: Aâ€“7 in all suits, plus two distinguishable Jokers (Canadian). US: no Jokers, trump 9 is top trump.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '34-card pack + 2 Jokers (or 32-card no Jokers); score sheet.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '8 cards each; dealer places 2 cards face down as kitty. Single round of bidding (left of dealer first, dealer last); bids must increase.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
